{{also|Scoop|-scoop}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|scope}}, {{m|enm|schoupe}}, a borrowing from {{der|en|dum|scoep}}, {{m|dum|scuep}}, {{m|dum|schope}}, {{m|dum|schoepe|t=bucket for bailing water}} and {{der|en|dum|schoppe}}, {{m|dum|scoppe}}, {{m|dum|schuppe}} {{gloss|"a scoop, shovel"; > Modern {{cog|nl|schop|t=spade}}}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*skuppǭ}}, {{m|gem-pro|*skuppijǭ}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)kep-|t=to cut, to scrape, to hack}}.<ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref>.

Cognate with {{cog|ofs|skuppe|t=shovel}}, {{cog|gml|schōpe|t=scoop, shovel}}, {{cog|nds-de|Schüppe}}, {{m|nds-de|Schüpp|t=shovel}}, {{cog|de|Schüppe}}, {{m|de|Schippe|t=shovel, spade}}. Related to {{cog|en|shovel}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|sko͞op}}, {{IPA|en|/skuːp/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-scoop.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːp|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any cup- or bowl-shaped tool, usually with a [[handle]], used to lift and move loose or soft solid material.
#: {{ux|en|She kept a '''scoop''' in the dog food.}}
#: {{ux|en|an ice-cream '''scoop'''}}
# The [[amount]] or [[volume]] of loose or solid material held by a particular scoop.
#: {{ux|en|Use one '''scoop''' of coffee for each pot.}}
#: {{ux|en|I'll have one '''scoop''' of chocolate ice-cream.}}
# The act of scooping, or taking with a scoop or ladle; a motion with a scoop, as in dipping or shovelling.
#: {{ux|en|with a quick '''scoop''', she fished the frog out of the pond.}}
# A [[story]] or [[fact]]; especially, news learned and reported before anyone else.
#: {{syn|en|dope|poop}}
#: {{ux|en|He listened carefully, in hopes of getting the '''scoop''' on the debate.}}
#* {{RQ:Doyle Lost World|passage="We may get a '''scoop''', if we are lucky. You'll be there in any case, so you'll just give us a pretty full report."}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2016-11-07|author=w:Peter Bradshaw|title=Allied: what happens when a film gets eclipsed by gossip|journal=w:The Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/film/2016/nov/07/allied-eclipsed-by-gossip-brad-pitt-marion-cotillard-hollywood|passage=The problem is that the public, disobediently giggling over their social media accounts, reckon they’ve already got the '''scoop''' without needing to see the film.}}
# {{lb|en|automotive}} An opening in a [[hood]]/[[bonnet]] or other [[body]] panel to admit air, usually for cooling the [[engine]].
# The digging attachment on a [[front-end loader]].
# A place hollowed out; a basinlike cavity; a hollow.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1819|author=w:Joseph Rodman Drake|title=s:The Culprit Fay
|passage=Some had lain in the '''scoop''' of the rock.}}
# A spoon-shaped [[surgical]] instrument, used in extracting certain substances or foreign bodies.
# A special spinal board used by [[EMS|emergency medical service]] staff that divides laterally to scoop up patients.
# A sweep; a stroke; a swoop.
# {{lb|en|Scotland}} The [[peak]] of a [[cap]].
# {{lb|en|pinball}} A hole on the [[playfield]] that catches a ball, but eventually returns it to play in one way or another.
# {{lb|en|surfing}} The raised end of a [[surfboard]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1965|author=John M. Kelly|title=Surf and Sea|page=116
|passage=This brings the '''scoop''' into play as additional wetted surface and slows the board due to its fore-and-aft curvature}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1977|author=Fred Hemmings|title=Surfing: Hawaii's Gift to the World of Sports|page=59
|passage=[T]he '''scoop''' or upward curvature in the front or nose section of a board is designed to keep the board from diving under the surface of the water when the surfer is catching a wave.}}
# {{lb|en|film|television}} A kind of [[floodlight]] with a [[reflector]].

